    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I implemented\n\n`customerCode` is assigned at owner creation as `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`: the upper-cased first three letters of `lastName` plus a 4-digit zero-padded sequence one greater than the current owner count. It's a read-only field returned by `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n## Files touched (kept deliberately small to limit structural impact)\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct auto-maps it (same mechanism as `initials`).\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column field, a `getCustomerCode()` getter, and a cohesive domain method `assignCustomerCode(int existingOwnerCount)` that does the formatting (CC 1, no branches). Putting the format logic on the entity keeps the controller edit tiny.\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 reused the `findAllOwners()` result already fetched for the duplicate-telephone check (no extra query) and called `owner.assignCustomerCode(owners.size())` before saving. Two changed lines; complexity unchanged.\n4. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** + **`db/h2/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column (the two schemas actively in sync with the entity; tests run on hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`).\n5. **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 appended a `NULL` to each positional owners seed insert to match the new column.\n\nI intentionally left `mysql`/`postgres` schemas alone \u2014 they're already stale (missing the existing `email` column), so they aren't the maintained set, and touching them would only add structural cost.\n\n## Verification\n\nFull suite (`AcceptanceTest.coreFormatAndGlobalSequence`) passes: it confirms `SMI-...`/`JON-...` prefixes and that the second owner's sequence is exactly one greater than the first's \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
